The local catalog revision is `47c1a94efec4584c69f5aaec4856e40c3789e80de555eb878e12976d11e1f127`. Static metadata processing recomputed its revision, all 585 detail hashes and the recorded size/hash of each of the ten locally delivered gzip manifests. The source catalog also matches the local RUN.json transfer anchor. These are local consistency observations; no cloud object existence/generation, download, authentication or product reader was exercised.

The primary manifests and catalog details contain exactly the same 146,743 distinct machine/source paths, with zero paths missing or extra. There are 585 directory/project identities, 457 with delivered source, 128 without delivered source, 589 preserved versions, 419 suggested starting versions and 38 entries needing an explicit choice. Parent/nested views overlap; these numbers are not unique application counts. Suggestions compare observed bytes/permissions and do not establish canonical promotion, owner approval or an atomic snapshot. Primary historical retry status counts must not be summed as final unavailable counts: final estate exceptions are 535, including 532 held credential-shaped paths, one unavailable directory, one unavailable stat and one held large-source candidate. No held path/content list is emitted.

The inventory records recognized Node, Rust, Swift/Xcode, Python, CMake/Make, container/Compose, Gradle, Dart, Go, Meson/Nix/Just markers and lockfile filenames per delivered version. Counts across views overlap. Filename evidence does not establish recipes, targets, executable commands, dependency resolution, native libraries, SDKs, signing assets, generated sources, tool versions or complete input closure. Empty lockfile lists mean no recognized delivered filename, not absence from the original project. No source archive contents, .env or credential files were opened. Unrecognized custom build conventions remain unknown. Every project's build readiness is UNESTABLISHED.

Full Git history, installed dependencies/SDKs, secret/held inputs, bulk media/models/data and cache/build outputs are excluded from the source-copy guarantee. Actual required exclusions must be resolved per project without assuming a secret is needed or available. The inventory separates the known Foundry integration source scope from Foundry-associated name hints and external/unknown ownership. Captured parent directories may contain external/substrate material. All active-directory states remain unknown and none is declared safe to alter.

Static bridge review confirms the separation between the Python browse/source-copy index and the transactional TypeScript library authority. `Catalog.project/version`, generation-pinned `CloudReader.fetch`, `restore`, `publish_exclusive` and `sync` are inspected contracts, not exercised interfaces. Prepared publication descriptors, source-only restoration, no-overlay destinations and workspace receipts do not prove runtime safety, build readiness, fleet activation or canonical authority. The existing SOURCE-REVIEW.md is attributed; current prior-review hash comparisons are identity evidence only. New source-review corrections were not made by this lane.

