## Capacity facts and limits

Permitted observations completed at **2026-10-18 03:06:27 UTC**, local date **2026-10-17**. Remote scope was existing BatchMode SSH aliases mac4/mac5 with retained strict host-key checks, host-key updates disabled, no forwarding or connection multiplexing. No source/hydration, full disk traversal, SpaceFS or other agent data access occurred.

| Surface | macOS build | Xcode plist version/build | APFS Data available | df capacity |
| --- | --- | --- | ---: | ---: |
| Local operator host | 26.5.1 / 25F80 | 26.5 / 24943 | 6,735,648 KiB (6.424 GiB) | 99% |
| Mac4 alias | 26.3 / 25D125 | 26.2 / 24553 | 17,316,584 KiB (16.514 GiB) | 97% |
| Mac5 alias | 27.0 / 26A5368g | 26.3 / 24587 | 18,448,704 KiB (17.594 GiB) | 96% |

Only four explicitly named directories per host were considered. Local du: Xcode cache 736 KiB, DerivedData 154,568 KiB, Archives 0 KiB. Mac4 Archives 133,088 KiB; Mac5 DerivedData 21,296 KiB. Other listed directories were missing-or-symlink and were not measured; that is not a claim of an empty directory or absent SDK elsewhere. FoundryLibrary cache was not measured on any host. No general cache scan was made.

Root/Data df available values describe shared APFS capacity and must not be added. du allocation is not independently reclaimable physical space; clones, snapshots, concurrent activity and retention can change the meaning. Xcode plist metadata establishes neither selected developer directory nor SDK/platform availability, license/first-launch status or build compatibility. No Xcode command ran. No CPU/RAM/daemon/hardware qualification was attempted. No current cache or archive, even in a Foundry-named namespace, is accepted as inactive or safe to delete. Accepted reclaimable capacity is zero.

Per-version restore lower bounds use referenced archive bytes + delivered source bytes + the existing pull code's 64 MiB margin. They are cold-source-copy estimates only: dependencies, toolchains, build outputs, failed stages, retention, concurrent pulls and an operating reserve are unbudgeted. Available disk does not establish build headroom on any host.

